1
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:11,309
it always strikes me how people think
about their presentations or how they

2
00:00:11,309 --> 00:00:15,990
prepare their presentations. I'm actually
talking about the first words

3
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:17,517
the first sentences of a presentation.

4
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:19,590
What most people do is
 they think of a presentation

5
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:24,029
so automatically you think
about a PowerPoint so you make your slides

6
00:00:24,029 --> 00:00:29,010
You look at your slides and you
think about what will I say showing each slide

7
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:34,860
But my question to you is this:
What are your first words?

8
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:38,850
What are your first sentences? Very few people
think about that just think a minute

9
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:42,239
about the presentations that you have
already seen in the past

10
00:00:42,239 --> 00:00:45,202
Maybe thepresentations that you have done
yourself

11
00:00:45,202 --> 00:00:47,039
There is a cliche sentence that

12
00:00:47,039 --> 00:00:52,020
most speakers use to introduce their
topic. They say something like

13
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:55,500
Good morning,  good afternoon, my name is ... (if
they don't know you)

14
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,300
and then there is this typical sentence

15
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,800
"Today I'm going to
talk to you about..."

16
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,180
Now you might say "so what's the problem?"

17
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:05,250
The problem with this
sentence is that you're actually

18
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:08,700
answering the wrong question you're
answering the WHAT question.

19
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:09,930
what are you going to do?

20
00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:15,570
I'm going to talk about.... 
If you think about it most audiences know

21
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:19,950
what you're going to talk about either
you are introduced or there is a program

22
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:24,900
or there is a meeting so there is an
agenda so people know what your topic is all about

23
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:30,360
The most interesting question
to answer is the WHY question

24
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:35,189
Why are you there to talk about this topic and
even more importantly why is it important

25
00:01:35,189 --> 00:01:41,200
for the audience to listen to you so my
advice for you is to focus on the WHY question

26
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:45,899
Now how can you do that? 
I advise people to focus on a story to

27
00:01:45,899 --> 00:01:51,000
begin their presentation. Now if you
think about stories, stories begin with a time frame

28
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,100
Just look at fairytales. 
They start with once upon a time ...

29
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:59,460
Im' not going to suggest that you start your
professional presentation with once upon

30
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:04,290
a time ... But you can start with a time
frame. Something like: Yesterday

31
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:09,209
Two weeks ago, Last year, Three months ago ...
Now what's the kind of story that you can

32
00:02:09,209 --> 00:02:13,350
share then? Use real stories. 
It has to be something that happened

33
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:18,600
to you. It has to be something that you
heard. So you can refer to a conversation

34
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:22,650
you had with a colleague. You can say
something like: Yesterday I had a

35
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:27,180
conversation with ... But then there has to
be a reason why you refer to that

36
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:31,710
conversation.  And there is this linking
sentence that I use in lots of

37
00:02:31,710 --> 00:02:36,480
presentations I tell my story and then I
continue saying: Now why do I tell you this?

38
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:42,000
Because my objective or my goal
with this presentation is to ...

39
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,310
So what you can do is be very conscious of the
company's stories I might say

40
00:02:47,310 --> 00:02:51,570
It can be something that happened with a customer,
it can be an article you read,

41
00:02:51,570 --> 00:02:56,000
it can be something that you heard about, 
it can be a conversation you had ...

42
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:03,000
So use these stories to begin your presentations,
link them to your goal and it will be so

43
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,500
much more interesting for your audience
because it will be crystal clear for them

44
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:11,000
from the very first minute why it
is important to them.

45
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:17,840
So next time you prepare your presentation 
focus on that WHY question and tell them a story

